  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b2643b01-11c1-5614-8abf-b55d9e289fd9" activityNameId="21a7f70a-eb77-5788-bb63-15b01c26f2e4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Printed wiring board mounting facilities, SMT type</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Printed wiring board mounting facilities, SMT type
The data represent an example of a SMT mounting line – comprising 3 small component placing machines, 2 big components placing machines, 1 inspection device and 1 reflow oven. Total weight data are taken from producer information of such machines. Composition, infrastructure and production efforts are based on own assumptions. The dataset represents a production line with a total weight of 19’300 kg. ICT dataset updates in 2023 were included in the inventory; UUID: 09943bd3-7019-3055-ab9f-a78eb2fd1750
This module includes material, production efforts (material treatment processes), transport efforts and the infrastructure for the production of all the machineries used for the mouning of surface mount components onto a printed wiring board. No information about emissions (air, water) and waste are included.
Location: Data represent a global valid composition of a SMT mounting line
Technology: Typical data of current machines sold for the mounting of SMD components (see general comments).
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_09943bd3-7019-3055-ab9f-a78eb2fd1750.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
